@startuml
title FrioTrack frontend modules and HTTP boundary
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
package "SPA" {
class WorkspaceApplication <<module>> {
  + data: Ref<WorkspaceData>
  + profile: Ref<Profile>
  + login(draft)
  + register(draft)
  + logout()
  + execute(type, payload)
  + restoreSession()
}
class ContextPresentation <<VuePagesAndRouter>>
ContextPresentation --> WorkspaceApplication : invokes use cases
abstract class WorkspaceGateway <<ApplicationPort>>
class RestWorkspaceGateway <<HttpAdapter>>
class ShipmentPolicies <<PureFunctions>>
class ThermalPolicies <<PureFunctions>>
class AccessPolicies <<PureFunctions>>
WorkspaceApplication --> WorkspaceGateway : depends on contract
RestWorkspaceGateway --|> WorkspaceGateway : implements
ContextPresentation ..> ShipmentPolicies
ContextPresentation ..> ThermalPolicies
ContextPresentation ..> AccessPolicies
}
class SupportingApi <<ASP.NET Core Container>>
RestWorkspaceGateway ..> SupportingApi : HTTPS JSON / opaque bearer
note bottom
Module view, not a claim of typed backend aggregates.
HTTP requests and session handling remain in the adapter.
Domain policies do not depend on Vue or persistence.
end note
@enduml
